// PORT-PENDING 2056 crates-jet-pkg-model-src-cffi-slice-1: crates/jet-pkg-model/src/CFFI.rs:1-1800
// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! S59 (E2-M14) — C FFI assembly, merge, and link resolution.
//RS //!
//RS //! The front end owns all C-FFI semantics; rustc only verifies the generated
//RS //! `extern "C"` shims (I2/I3). This module runs after the loader has read every
//RS //! `.jet` file and before sema:
//RS //!
//RS //! 1. Gather every `#Import module c.<lib>` (overlay) and
//RS //!    `#Bindgen module c.<lib>.__bindgen__` (generated cache) item.
//RS //! 2. Enforce the location rule: `#Bindgen` only in a generated
//RS //!    `.jet/bindings/c/<lib>.jet` file (E3207).
//RS //! 3. Merge per library — **bindgen ∪ overlay, overlay wins** on a clash;
//RS //!    incompatible signatures are E3205 (D-CFFI2-SYN-4).
//RS //! 4. Materialize one synthetic module per library (alias `__c_<lib>`) holding
//RS //!    the merged surface, so the rest of the pipeline treats C calls exactly
//RS //!    like any other namespaced module call.
//RS //! 5. Classify each file's C `use` forms — `use c.<lib>` / `use "<header>.h"` —
//RS //!    one form per lib per file (E3204), and record the synthetic target for
//RS //!    sema's import map.
//RS //!
//RS //! Link discovery lives in helpers here: a declared `<lib>: c@…` dep in the
//RS //! `deps:` block of `package.jet` (S59/D-CFFI2) takes precedence, else `pkg-config
//RS //! <lib>`, else E3201.
//RS 
